          "question": "Drawing on Lesson 1: a hurricane disrupts gasoline supply in Florida. Stations raise prices from $3.50 to $5.50. Politicians call for anti-price-gouging laws. What does economic analysis suggest?",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "Price caps will help everyone by keeping fuel affordable",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "The price spike, while painful, performs critical functions: signaling scarcity, rationing fuel, and incentivizing supply",
              "correct": true
            },
            {
              "text": "The market is broken and government should set fair prices",
              "correct": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Higher prices have no effect because demand is fixed in emergencies",
              "correct": false
            }
          ],
          "explanation": "This is the supply-and-demand lesson applied to a real emergency. High prices serve three critical functions: (1) signaling extreme scarcity, (2) rationing limited supply to highest-value uses (e.g., evacuating families), (3) incentivizing distant suppliers to truck fuel in. Price caps cause shortages, lines, and informal rationing. Economists across the political spectrum largely agree that anti-gouging laws backfire — though they remain politically popular because the visible 'unfairness' is more salient than the invisible empty pumps.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quiz: Hurricane Gas Prices</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#999\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apply Lesson 1: supply &amp; demand</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"200\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Three Functions of Prices</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Signal scarcity</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Ration limited supply</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"425\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Incentivize distant supply (trucks roll in)</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"490\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Anti-Gouging Laws Cause</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shortages and lines</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Informal/black-market rationing</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No price signal to bring in supply</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"685\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#999\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Florida 1992 Andrew, 2017 Irma showed both</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"730\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"775\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why Are They Popular?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"820\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Empty pumps are invisible</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">$5.50 price tag is visible</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"910\" width=\"900\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"955\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Better Policy</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Direct cash aid to affected families</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1035\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Let prices do their job</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Prices ration scarce resources. Caps cause shortages. Help people directly instead."
          }
